\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16200 \cf2 \cb3 What this course is\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa303\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs30\fsmilli15200 \cf2 AI has made it far easier to turn an idea into something real. It has not made anyone better at deciding what is worth making, or at telling good work from bad. That part is still human, and it is what this course works on.\
This is a studio course. We will use AI as a working medium for three connected capacities:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Cognition:
\f1\b0  noticing, framing, questioning, evaluating, and choosing.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Communication:
\f1\b0  expressing intent clearly enough that humans and machines can work with it.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Creativity:
\f1\b0  making possibilities tangible, encountering what happens, and revising.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa303\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 The course is structured around a stable weekly rhythm. Examples, tools, guests, and project briefs may change as the class develops; the learning contract and grading structure will not change without clear notice.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa268\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16200 \cf2 Learning outcomes\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa303\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs30\fsmilli15200 \cf2 By the end of the course, students should be able to:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Turn an ambiguous interest into a clear intention and workable next step.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Collaborate with AI across ideation, research, prototyping, debugging, revision, and critique.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Create and share a series of artifacts using tools appropriate to the work.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Describe their process, decisions, failures, and learning in their own words.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Give, receive, and use feedback in a studio community.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Evaluate AI output for quality, limits, consequences, and effects on other people.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Develop a personal building practice that can continue beyond this course.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa268\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16200 \cf2 \cb3 The weekly studio rhythm\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa303\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs30\fsmilli15200 \cf2 Every week, everyone makes something and writes a short account of what actually happened. Each weekly submission has three parts:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Artifact:
\f1\b0  Make something another person can encounter. It may be small, unfinished, or strange. Depending on the week, it could be an app, image, story, analysis, event plan, automation, performance, dataset, physical object, workflow, or another form proposed by the student.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Reflection:
\f1\b0  Write at least one paragraph in your own words describing what you tried, what you actually did, what changed or failed, and what you learned. Prompts will be provided. One paragraph is the minimum, not the target \'97 write more whenever there is more to say. Grammar and polish are not being graded; what you are practicing is how well you can articulate what happened.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Studio share:
\f1\b0  On September 14 everyone demos, after two weeks of building. From then on demos alternate \'97 roughly half the class shares each week, so every demo gets real time and real attention. On your demo week, you may share whatever you are working on: this week's artifact, an older project you kept going with, or a place you are stuck and want the room's help. On your off weeks the work is just as active: asking questions and offering usable feedback is how a studio runs.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa303\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 A failed experiment with a clear reflection can score better than a polished artifact whose maker cannot explain their choices.\
Weekly submissions (artifact + reflection) are due in Canvas by 
\f0\b Sunday at midnight (11:59 PM)
\f1\b0 , the night before class, so each Monday session can respond to what the room actually made and wants to learn next.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa268\partightenfactor0

